1
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:06,010
[FRENCI] These remnants
are all we managed to salvage.

2
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:08,510
We discovered them
in the guild fireplace.

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:11,140
Everything else
had already turned to ash.

4
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,510
[Kivia exhales softly]

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,100
[KIVIA] What's this?

6
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:19,020
Most likely a contract receipt.

7
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:23,060
[Kivia breathes shakily]

8
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:26,400
His name is Mahaeyzel Zelkoff.

9
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:29,990
[KIVIA] It's imperative that
we get him into custody.

10
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:32,570
[FRENCI] I doubt
that will be possible.

11
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:35,540
I imagine he's already
left this town behind.

12
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:37,330
One way or another.

13
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:43,080
[RAJIT] Permission denied.

14
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:45,210
I don't have the authorization.

15
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:48,880
I'm aware your hands are bound
by the ropes of bureaucracy.

16
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:50,970
But, look, our circumstances
have changed.

17
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:54,600
I come bearing a special order
for his immediate release.

18
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:56,260
[Rajit sighs]

19
00:00:56,310 --> 00:00:58,310
I'm to believe this is genuine?

20
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:00,060
[VENETIM] There can be no doubt.

21
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:02,480
It has the glorious seal
of Galtuile.

22
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:05,730
The local military supervisor
was very accommodating.

23
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:09,360
Oh, naturally, you're free
to confirm its veracity.

24
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:10,570
Though locking up a hero

25
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:12,700
hardly seems a punishment
to begin with.

26
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,370
It's more like a holiday.

27
00:01:14,410 --> 00:01:15,910
He's sleeping blissfully,

28
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:19,330
resting in safety and security
while we others risk it all.

29
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:21,710
Am I wrong?

30
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:23,170
[Rajit sighs]

31
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:26,460
Wait here a minute.

32
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,630
I'll go confirm.

33
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:29,510
By all means, do!

34
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:33,220
[♪ opening theme song playing]

35
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:01,930
♪

36
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,520
[indistinct chatter]

37
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,060
[TEORITTA] My knight,
your divine muse

38
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,110
desires an outing.

39
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:10,480
Does your heart
not ache to explore?

40
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:13,690
Your love of zeff butter
is becoming an obsession.

41
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:16,160
I shall not suffer
further confinement here.

42
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:18,530
I wish to go outside! [grunts]

43
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:20,740
Well, that's not
our call to make.

44
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:22,790
[NORGALLE]
If the goddess wants an outing,

45
00:03:22,830 --> 00:03:24,290
I can think
of nothing more fitting

46
00:03:24,330 --> 00:03:26,460
than a trip to the
Dujin Art Museum.

47
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:29,130
It boasts a collection
of masterpieces

48
00:03:29,170 --> 00:03:30,670
from the middle classical era,

49
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,550
while the building itself
showcases

50
00:03:32,590 --> 00:03:35,130
modern Nashida
architectural techniques.

51
00:03:35,170 --> 00:03:36,880
Truly a visual triumph!

52
00:03:36,930 --> 00:03:39,090
Naturally,
as a strategic port...

53
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:41,850
What's there to like about
a dusty old museum?

54
00:03:41,890 --> 00:03:43,850
Nothing can beat the ocean.

55
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,890
The view's great
as you fly out to sea.

56
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:49,520
And aerial hunting in the forest
is always fun.

57
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,730
[XYLO] Not everyone can fly,
you know.

58
00:03:51,770 --> 00:03:53,320
At least suggest something

59
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,440
that someone who isn't a dragon
would enjoy.

60
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,820
What, you don't care
if dragons are happy?

61
00:03:57,860 --> 00:03:59,990
My knight,
any activity would suffice.

62
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:02,080
I simply wish
to go into town today!

63
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,450
Out of the question.

64
00:04:03,490 --> 00:04:04,540
Or have you forgotten

65
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:06,330
that you have
a target on your back?

66
00:04:06,370 --> 00:04:08,540
I doubt that they'll ever
let us out again.

67
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:09,750
[Teoritta groans]

68
00:04:09,790 --> 00:04:11,630
How very disheartening.

69
00:04:11,670 --> 00:04:12,750
[KIVIA] It's fine.

70
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:14,460
I can grant you permission.

71
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:15,710
[TEORITTA] Is that so?

72
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:18,220
But you can't go any further
than the Temple.

73
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,760
It's close to the barracks.

74
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,140
I'll arrange a full security
detail for you.

75
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:25,640
Kivia, on occasion, you are
the herald of good tidings!

76
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:27,350
To what do we owe all these?

77
00:04:27,390 --> 00:04:30,020
Yeah? Well, I'm guessing
there's some reason.

78
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:31,270
There isn't.

79
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:34,070
I'm simply hoping to brighten
goddess Teoritta's day

80
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:35,270
in whatever way I can.

81
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,860
[TEORITTA] How admirable!

82
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:39,360
Xylo, you should seek
to curry my favor as well.

83
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,740
[XYLO] You can't just
demand that.

84
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,200
It's settled.

85
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:46,250
Inform High Priest Marlen
of the plan.

86
00:04:46,290 --> 00:04:49,660
I'll send a unit
of my most trustworthy soldiers.

87
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:52,250
[XYLO] You won't be joining us?

88
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,210
[KIVIA] Not today.

89
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:58,630
-[Teoritta exclaiming, grunting]
-[KIVIA] I'm busy.

90
00:04:58,670 --> 00:04:59,880
Understood.

91
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:02,180
And I will be sure to keep
a close eye on Teoritta.

92
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,720
[indistinct chatter]

93
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,020
♪

94
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:08,180
[GIRL 1] It's really her!

95
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:10,480
[BOY 1] The Great Goddess
of Swords, Teoritta!

96
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:12,440
Goddess, can you sign my tunic?

97
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:14,230
I'd love for you
to sign my book, too!

98
00:05:14,270 --> 00:05:16,070
[TEORITTA]
Your prayers are answered!

99
00:05:16,110 --> 00:05:18,150
Ample blessings shall now be
bestowed upon you

100
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:20,610
by the grace
of the great goddess Teoritta!

101
00:05:20,650 --> 00:05:22,490
-[GIRL 1] Hooray!
-[BOY 2] Do mine next!

102
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,370
[GIRL 2] I want
your blessing too, Goddess!

103
00:05:24,410 --> 00:05:25,950
According to superstition,

104
00:05:25,990 --> 00:05:28,700
a goddess' signature
wards off bad luck.

105
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:31,290
I guess some people
still believe in that.

106
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:33,170
Well, it seems harmless.

107
00:05:33,210 --> 00:05:34,420
[Teoritta hums]

108
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:36,000
-[WOMAN] Blessed goddess.
-Oh?

109
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:38,590
Here, we brought you
some nice treats.

110
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:41,220
You're the same size
as my sweet little grandchild,

111
00:05:41,260 --> 00:05:44,140
and yet you go around fighting
Demon Blights on our behalf.

112
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:45,850
[TEORITTA]
Ah, there is nothing to it!

113
00:05:45,890 --> 00:05:47,760
Not for a truly mighty goddess!

114
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:49,310
Are you watching this,
my knight?

115
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:51,390
Such is the appropriate
treatment of a goddess,

116
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:53,520
which you should
pridefully seek to mimic.

117
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,610
But, first, you may
partake of my treats!

118
00:05:55,650 --> 00:05:57,190
You're too generous.

119
00:05:57,230 --> 00:05:59,400
Though, I should check
for poison.

120
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:00,690
I'm sorry, ma'am...

121
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:01,780
Isn't that the
Demon Lord hunter...

122
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,610
...but I'll have to
confiscate these.

123
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:04,740
The Thunder Falcon!

124
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,740
His name's Xylo Forbartz,
and I really

125
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:08,080
-want his autograph!
-What?

126
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:09,660
All these people
know about me, too?

127
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:10,910
-[MARLEN] They do.
-Uh?

128
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:13,460
[MARLEN] You're quite popular
these days.

129
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:15,540
High Priest Marlen.

130
00:06:16,130 --> 00:06:18,090
Rumors have a way of spreading.

131
00:06:18,130 --> 00:06:20,460
They know about your deeds
at Mureed Fortress

132
00:06:20,510 --> 00:06:21,880
and Sodrick's Shell.

133
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:24,930
[laughs] But I'm just
a lowly penal hero.

134
00:06:24,970 --> 00:06:26,050
[overlapping chatter]

135
00:06:26,590 --> 00:06:29,010
[MARLEN] I doubt these children
can yet grasp what that means.

136
00:06:29,060 --> 00:06:32,180
As for myself,
I've had cause to reevaluate.

137
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:35,230
My niece has told me
a great deal about you.

138
00:06:36,650 --> 00:06:39,650
Patausche may be too noble
for her own good.

139
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:42,900
She values honor
above even her own well-being.

140
00:06:43,610 --> 00:06:47,120
A desire to be remembered
for great deeds, I suppose.

141
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:50,450
Rather troubling,
don't you agree?

142
00:06:50,490 --> 00:06:51,830
Perhaps.

143
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,750
There are more like her
than you'd think.

144
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:57,750
Especially fighting the battle
against the Demon Blight.

145
00:06:58,170 --> 00:07:01,000
Though, I'm sure it's harder
when it's your own niece.

146
00:07:01,050 --> 00:07:02,050
True.

147
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:04,260
I have always cared
for Patausche

148
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:06,260
as though she were
my own daughter.

149
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:10,060
If anyone were to betray her
or cause her undue sorrow,

150
00:07:10,470 --> 00:07:12,270
I would intervene.

151
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:14,060
[XYLO] Uh...

152
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:16,230
Listen, Xylo Forbartz,

153
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:18,270
I have heard
that you have a fiancée...

154
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:19,770
-[bell tolling]
-[both gasp]

155
00:07:19,810 --> 00:07:22,150
-[MAN 1] The bell!
-[MAN 2] That could only mean...

156
00:07:22,730 --> 00:07:25,440
-[Xylo grunts]
-Xylo, what does it portend?

157
00:07:25,490 --> 00:07:26,950
-[MARLEN] An attack.
-[Teoritta gasps]

158
00:07:26,990 --> 00:07:29,910
When those bells
are rung in Ioff City,

159
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:32,620
it means we are under siege.

160
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,200
[bell tolling in distance]

161
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:38,630
[KIVIA] Uh?

162
00:07:40,170 --> 00:07:41,250
[VENETIM] Uh?

163
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:44,010
Greetings! I wasn't expecting
company.

164
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:46,840
Enough.
What are you doing in here?

165
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,090
[VENETIM] Me?

166
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:51,310
I realized I had made a mistake
in a recent report,

167
00:07:51,350 --> 00:07:53,680
so I figured I should
try to correct it.

168
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,730
Are you aware
that crucial military

169
00:07:55,770 --> 00:07:58,310
and Temple documents
are stored in this room?

170
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:00,730
Only officers
are permitted to enter.

171
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:02,940
Oh, I had no idea!

172
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:05,280
I must humbly
beg your forgiveness.

173
00:08:07,450 --> 00:08:10,320
Prepare for combat,
and stay out of this place.

174
00:08:10,370 --> 00:08:11,450
But of course!

175
00:08:11,490 --> 00:08:13,410
I'll go assemble
the Hero Unit at once.

176
00:08:13,450 --> 00:08:14,490
I do hope

177
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,870
we can keep this
little incident between us.

178
00:08:16,910 --> 00:08:18,330
[steps receding]

179
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:21,210
[door opens, closes]

180
00:08:27,670 --> 00:08:28,760
[grunts softly]

181
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:36,930
[VENETIM] I wish you'd
consider the fact

182
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:38,600
that I have to
free you every time

183
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,560
you get yourself locked up.

184
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:43,440
Oh? I didn't know
you were back.

185
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,530
Well, hello there, Xylo.

186
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:49,240
I'm glad to see you're thriving.

187
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:51,280
I hear you've been
having quite a time

188
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,620
while I was locked away.

189
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:55,530
My heart broke for you
from within my prison cell.

190
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:58,290
Yet somehow you're just
as smug as you always are.

191
00:08:58,330 --> 00:08:59,910
And who do we have here?

192
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:02,460
The famous goddess, correct?

193
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,840
[Teoritta grunts softly]

194
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:06,090
[RHYNO] It is truly
an honor to meet you.

195
00:09:06,130 --> 00:09:08,010
The name is Rhyno.

196
00:09:08,050 --> 00:09:12,340
I proudly serve as the artillery
for Penal Hero Unit 9004.

197
00:09:12,390 --> 00:09:15,510
In fact, you could say that
Comrade Xylo and I are partners.

198
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:16,520
[Xylo grunts softly]

199
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:18,230
We're nothing of the sort.

200
00:09:18,770 --> 00:09:20,440
Hey, Venetim,
I'm starting to think

201
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:22,400
we busted him out
way too early.

202
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,860
Just looking at the bastard

203
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,150
-pisses me off.
-[gasps]

204
00:09:25,190 --> 00:09:27,730
You're the one who insisted
I get him released!

205
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:29,030
[XYLO] A volunteer hero

206
00:09:29,070 --> 00:09:31,200
who keeps getting
thrown in a cell?

207
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:32,910
What the hell
were you thinking?

208
00:09:32,950 --> 00:09:34,490
I wanted to help,

209
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:36,990
to be of service
to the poor, vulnerable souls

210
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:38,540
getting trampled by faeries,

211
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:41,370
which is why I had no choice
but to do what I did.

212
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:43,080
[XYLO] "Had no choice"

213
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:45,920
but to shell civilian houses
into oblivion?

214
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,340
-That makes no damn sense.
-[RHYNO] Agree to disagree.

215
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:51,050
For now, might I suggest
we join forces

216
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:54,140
and fight our way through this
latest round of trouble.

217
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:55,850
Anyway...

218
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:58,640
Ioff Cheg is the Port district.

219
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:01,640
It seems that's where
the faeries first originated.

220
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:05,230
The horde then moved on
to this location.

221
00:10:05,270 --> 00:10:08,780
That's where they occupied
Tui Jia, the Coral Tower.

222
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:12,200
[grunts] A key part
of our coastal defense.

223
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:14,490
[explosion]

224
00:10:15,070 --> 00:10:17,280
[VENETIM] The horde
has a Demon Lord with it,

225
00:10:17,330 --> 00:10:18,870
which could taint Tui Jia

226
00:10:18,910 --> 00:10:20,870
until it transforms
into a faerie.

227
00:10:20,910 --> 00:10:22,540
-It's a trap.
-It's clearly a trap.

228
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,290
-[Xylo grunts]
-[Rhyno chuckles]

229
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:26,670
[RHYNO] They've got
artillery too, right?

230
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:28,380
Given the wind direction
and speed,

231
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:30,590
you could hit anywhere
in Ioff Cheg from there,

232
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:32,340
meaning they have
the advantage.

233
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:36,220
[XYLO] They're basically holding
this whole region hostage.

234
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,220
What are Galtuile's orders?

235
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,770
[VENETIM] Ah, well.
Funny you should ask.

236
00:10:40,810 --> 00:10:43,180
The Thirteenth Order
of the Holy Knights

237
00:10:43,230 --> 00:10:44,310
and the Ioff City Guard

238
00:10:44,390 --> 00:10:46,610
will be stationed
in the Inland district,

239
00:10:46,650 --> 00:10:49,190
while the Hero Unit
will act as the sole defense

240
00:10:49,230 --> 00:10:50,280
of the Port district.

241
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,320
[XYLO] Huh?

242
00:10:51,690 --> 00:10:54,150
We're told to hold out
until reinforcements arrive,

243
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,570
at which point,
they'll begin a counterattack.

244
00:10:56,620 --> 00:10:57,660
Got it?

245
00:10:58,070 --> 00:10:59,450
That's their big plan?

246
00:10:59,490 --> 00:11:02,160
To abandon everyone
living in the Port district?

247
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:04,790
The Noble Alliance
was always going to prioritize

248
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:06,000
the Inland district!

249
00:11:06,170 --> 00:11:08,080
That's where most of their
government facilities

250
00:11:08,130 --> 00:11:10,420
and noble properties
are located.

251
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:14,170
[XYLO] Dammit, they only care
about themselves.

252
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:17,220
Xylo, there's no point
in getting hurt or killed

253
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:18,890
for a hopeless mission
like this,

254
00:11:18,930 --> 00:11:20,600
-and you know I'm right.
-[XYLO] Meaning?

255
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:21,720
Perhaps we should strive

256
00:11:21,810 --> 00:11:24,140
to avoid doing anything
overly aggressive.

257
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:26,560
[TEORITTA] Have you
no concept of shame?

258
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:29,440
Regardless of the trials
we face, rejoice!

259
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,900
For we have
the immense honor

260
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,610
of being the sole guardians
of the people.

261
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:36,150
And such battles are well worth
laying down our very lives for!

262
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:38,200
Stop. I already told you

263
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,910
to get over your bent
for self-sacrifice-

264
00:11:39,950 --> 00:11:41,780
[RHYNO]
What a magnificent goddess!

265
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:44,790
Your willingness to die
for the cause is inspiring,

266
00:11:44,830 --> 00:11:46,410
and I completely agree.

267
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:50,040
Comrade Xylo, the time has come
to lend our strength.

268
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,710
Let us join hands and fight

269
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:54,260
for the hopes and dreams
of these fine people!

270
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:55,420
Enough already.

271
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:57,180
It's not as though
we have a choice.

272
00:11:57,220 --> 00:12:00,140
Xylo, I am certain
you shall forge a path.

273
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:02,180
I have
the utmost faith in you.

274
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,640
[grunts] I'm aware.

275
00:12:04,970 --> 00:12:07,190
Good thing I refuse
to let those assholes

276
00:12:07,230 --> 00:12:08,520
have their way.

277
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:11,440
They'll regret
underestimating me.

278
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:13,690
♪

279
00:12:14,190 --> 00:12:16,240
This site shall be
our stronghold!

280
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:18,530
A sanctuary
for those evacuating.

281
00:12:18,570 --> 00:12:20,780
Let us construct
a sacred seal fence

282
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:22,490
in accordance
with my blueprints.

283
00:12:22,530 --> 00:12:23,540
[ADVENTURERS] Majesty!

284
00:12:23,830 --> 00:12:25,500
[NORGALLE] Then we harness
the burning embers!

285
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:26,580
Gather all the food

286
00:12:26,830 --> 00:12:28,870
and sacred seal-infused
cookware you can find.

287
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:30,080
[ADVENTURERS] On it!

288
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,750
Hold on. What are those
guild people doing here?

289
00:12:32,790 --> 00:12:35,960
Apparently, His Majesty promised
he would give them some work.

290
00:12:36,010 --> 00:12:39,090
Pretty sure he said something
about salaries and titles.

291
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:40,510
Titles, huh?

292
00:12:40,970 --> 00:12:43,220
The first thing we'll do
is gather some wood!

293
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:45,100
As much as your arms
can carry!

294
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:46,350
-[ADVENTURERS] Yes, sir.
-[COMMANDER] Hurry up.

295
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:47,730
Figures. Though,
I guess it's better

296
00:12:47,770 --> 00:12:49,640
than them becoming highwaymen.

297
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,650
[indistinct chatter]

298
00:12:58,570 --> 00:13:00,450
[gobbling]

299
00:13:00,490 --> 00:13:02,990
[TEORITTA]
It is very hot but very good!

300
00:13:03,030 --> 00:13:04,160
Hey, Tatsuya,

301
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,370
eat up!

302
00:13:08,710 --> 00:13:11,170
You dunce! Not with your hands!

303
00:13:11,210 --> 00:13:13,080
To rush is sheer folly.

304
00:13:13,130 --> 00:13:15,630
So you know, you're spilling
as much as he is.

305
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:17,130
[footsteps]

306
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,130
[Teoritta grunts]

307
00:13:19,630 --> 00:13:22,010
[RHYNO] Nothing invigorates
the spirit like a hot meal.

308
00:13:22,050 --> 00:13:24,970
Placing top priority
on securing a way to cook...

309
00:13:25,010 --> 00:13:27,270
Norgalle is a born leader.

310
00:13:27,310 --> 00:13:28,850
Quite impressive!

311
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:31,690
My... his garb is most unusual.

312
00:13:31,730 --> 00:13:34,310
The Neven Artillery
Seal Compound.

313
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:35,610
That's what it's called,

314
00:13:35,770 --> 00:13:38,690
but I don't know why he's chosen
to wear it to dinner.

315
00:13:40,190 --> 00:13:42,820
I was hoping we'd have
the whole unit back together

316
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:44,030
at long last.

317
00:13:44,070 --> 00:13:45,870
I take it we will be reuniting

318
00:13:45,910 --> 00:13:47,910
with the rest
of our comrades shortly?

319
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,830
Tsav is currently getting
his arm repaired.

320
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:52,750
But considering
the circumstances,

321
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,250
they'll likely do
the bare minimum

322
00:13:54,290 --> 00:13:55,630
before deploying him.

323
00:13:55,670 --> 00:13:56,840
[Tsav screams]

324
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:58,460
And Comrade Jayce?

325
00:13:58,510 --> 00:14:00,840
I'm quite surprised
he isn't already here.

326
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:03,640
[XYLO] Venetim's working
on it as we speak.

327
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:04,840
They think sending a dragon

328
00:14:04,890 --> 00:14:06,890
for urban warfare
is too dangerous,

329
00:14:06,930 --> 00:14:08,430
but he'll convince them.

330
00:14:08,770 --> 00:14:10,930
I doubt His Majesty
will leave the base.

331
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:14,150
And Dotta's more useful
for scouting than fighting.

332
00:14:14,190 --> 00:14:17,150
So it's just the four of us
heading to Tui Jia.

333
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:18,940
Goes without saying...

334
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:22,530
That's not gonna be
nearly enough manpower.

335
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:26,370
[RHYNO] If I may,
I have a suggestion.

336
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:29,490
[XYLO] Do I even want to know?

337
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:32,160
[RHYNO] I could always shell
that massive wall down.

338
00:14:32,210 --> 00:14:34,960
The Inland District would
quickly be flooded with faeries,

339
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,710
effectively forcing
the other soldiers

340
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:37,750
to join the fight.

341
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,960
Thus, solving
our manpower issue.

342
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:41,630
[Teoritta grunts softly]

343
00:14:41,670 --> 00:14:43,590
[RHYNO] I believe
pain and suffering

344
00:14:43,630 --> 00:14:45,930
should be shared equally
among everyone.

345
00:14:45,970 --> 00:14:47,970
Humans tend
to bond over strife,

346
00:14:48,010 --> 00:14:49,850
so it's beautiful
when you think about it.

347
00:14:50,770 --> 00:14:52,270
Take heed, my knight.

348
00:14:52,310 --> 00:14:55,230
-That man is...
-Yeah, I'm aware.

349
00:14:55,270 --> 00:14:56,520
Denied.

350
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:59,190
Your moronic plan would
also endanger civilians.

351
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:00,230
[RHYNO] Hmm?

352
00:15:00,570 --> 00:15:03,240
Do you have a better idea
in mind, Comrade Xylo?

353
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:04,570
[XYLO] Rhyno,

354
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:07,700
most people aren't motivated
by the bonds they've formed.

355
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,410
But by profit.

356
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,580
Attack the ships
moored in the harbor.

357
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,870
I assume you can hit them
from here.

358
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,590
[RHYNO] I see, how brilliant.

359
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:20,420
Well done, Comrade Xylo.

360
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:23,300
After that, we go there.

361
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:27,510
We'll take back Tui Jia,
and murder the Demon Lord.

362
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:36,390
[knocking on door]

363
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,600
[RAJIT] Captain Kivia,

364
00:15:37,650 --> 00:15:39,900
we need your instructions
for the mission.

365
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:42,190
All right. I'm on my way.

366
00:15:44,490 --> 00:15:45,610
[Kivia sighs]

367
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:48,240
A foolish order,
no matter how you spin it.

368
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,620
Our hands are tied.

369
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:52,030
Maintaining the support
of the nobility is paramount,

370
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,830
and there are a lot
of Temple buildings

371
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:55,710
over in that district as well.

372
00:15:55,750 --> 00:15:56,750
[door opens]

373
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:59,710
Oops, I'm sorry
for interrupting.

374
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,170
Why are you here?

375
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:02,500
It was my understanding

376
00:16:02,550 --> 00:16:04,670
that the Hero Unit
was out in the field.

377
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:05,800
They are.

378
00:16:06,010 --> 00:16:08,050
As their commander,
I would love nothing more

379
00:16:08,090 --> 00:16:10,600
than to be there
rallying their spirits.

380
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:12,930
But instead,
I must woefully report

381
00:16:12,970 --> 00:16:14,220
that the faeries
have attacked

382
00:16:14,270 --> 00:16:16,350
the sacred seal vessels
in the harbor.

383
00:16:16,390 --> 00:16:17,600
They what?

384
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,770
I imagine the loss
of Temple property

385
00:16:19,810 --> 00:16:21,480
is simply unacceptable.

386
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:23,900
Which is why, I would like
to ask permission

387
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:25,320
to deploy our dragon.

388
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:26,490
You're lying.

389
00:16:26,530 --> 00:16:28,070
Why would the faeries
start by attacking

390
00:16:28,110 --> 00:16:29,700
-sacred seal vessels?
-[door opens]

391
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:33,450
Captain, a sacred seal vessel
is on fire!

392
00:16:33,490 --> 00:16:34,700
[Rajit sighs]

393
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,370
[SOLDIER] New orders.

394
00:16:36,410 --> 00:16:38,500
The Temple's requesting
our help.

395
00:16:40,170 --> 00:16:41,210
Thank you.

396
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,790
-You're dismissed.
-Right!

397
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:46,090
[door opens]

398
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:49,050
I see. You were telling
the truth, then.

399
00:16:49,090 --> 00:16:50,380
[VENETIM] I'm afraid so.

400
00:16:50,430 --> 00:16:52,470
I also found it
difficult to believe

401
00:16:52,510 --> 00:16:54,310
when I first heard the news.

402
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:56,470
It is a crying shame, isn't it?

403
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,810
[KIVIA] Very well.

404
00:16:59,850 --> 00:17:01,940
Your unit can use its dragon.

405
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:03,060
Is that wise?

406
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:05,860
[KIVIA] The Temple's request
is all the reason we need.

407
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:08,070
We'll also send some soldiers.

408
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:11,030
Your generosity is
more than appreciated.

409
00:17:11,070 --> 00:17:12,660
Really, thank you.

410
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:13,870
One last thing,

411
00:17:13,910 --> 00:17:16,080
please give my regards
to High Priest Marlen.

412
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:17,290
[Kivia grunts]

413
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:20,290
Go on. What are you saying?

414
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:22,250
Uh... Oh, I was merely-

415
00:17:22,290 --> 00:17:25,420
You don't even know him!
What are you insinuating?

416
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:27,760
Hear me out!
I wasn't trying...

417
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:30,420
Sheer insolence!

418
00:17:30,470 --> 00:17:33,050
High Priest Marlen
is a man of honor!

419
00:17:33,090 --> 00:17:35,390
He's devoted his whole life
to the Temple,

420
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:38,100
and he's always supported
the Holy Knights!

421
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:41,020
Yet despite that, you dare-

422
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:44,730
Please. You have it wrong.
Look, I can explain.

423
00:17:45,150 --> 00:17:46,730
It's simple, really.

424
00:17:46,770 --> 00:17:49,070
I have some advice
about security

425
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:52,070
-in the underground waterway.
-[Kivia gasps, grunts]

426
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,700
[Rajit gasps]

427
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:57,580
[exhales sharply]

428
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,120
[all clamoring]

429
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,710
[monsters growling]

430
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:06,340
[clamoring continues]

431
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:07,880
[MAN] Get to the shelter!

432
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:11,760
Xylo, they're coming.

433
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,800
Bogies! From the side, too!

434
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:15,600
-You're surrounded!
-[XYLO] Got it.

435
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:17,390
Keep a close eye
on our situation.

436
00:18:18,350 --> 00:18:19,640
Here we go!

437
00:18:19,930 --> 00:18:22,100
[growling]

438
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:24,400
[RHYNO] Look who's
come out to play.

439
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,690
Bogies are the bane
of artillerymen.

440
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:28,940
Comrade Xylo, if you don't mind.

441
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:31,280
-Tatsuya!
-[Tatsuya grunts]

442
00:18:34,070 --> 00:18:35,870
[Tatsuya yelling]

443
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:40,330
Let's get in there too,
Teoritta.

444
00:18:40,370 --> 00:18:43,460
Yes, I shall now
grant you my blessing!

445
00:18:54,630 --> 00:18:56,010
[XYLO] Time to die!

446
00:18:58,890 --> 00:19:00,720
[RHYNO]
Nothing is more exhilarating

447
00:19:00,770 --> 00:19:02,430
than fighting alongside
a comrade!

448
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:05,060
-Oh, I'm terribly lucky!
-[Xylo scoffs]

449
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:07,350
[XYLO] Keep running.
We'll charge our way

450
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:08,690
-to Tui Jia-
-[DOTTA] Hold on!

451
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:11,150
There is some kind of
warehouse up ahead.

452
00:19:11,190 --> 00:19:12,230
You should know.

453
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:14,860
It looks like it has
a Verkle Corp mark on it,

454
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:16,450
and the braziers are lit.

455
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:18,490
I think people
are holed up inside.

456
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:20,410
The faeries are swarming it.

457
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:22,240
They made a damn shelter?

458
00:19:22,290 --> 00:19:24,000
That timing couldn't be worse!

459
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:26,620
[RHYNO] What's our next plan
of attack, Comrade Xylo?

460
00:19:26,670 --> 00:19:30,960
My knight, to aid those people
would be most honorable.

461
00:19:31,710 --> 00:19:33,130
Would it not?

462
00:19:33,670 --> 00:19:34,590
I hear you.

463
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:35,760
-[growling]
-What the...

464
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,300
[monsters growling]

465
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:47,190
Rhyno, might end up
being a fight to the death.

466
00:19:47,230 --> 00:19:48,480
Prepare yourself.

467
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:50,360
[RHYNO] I'm always prepared.

468
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:53,190
To protect the nameless masses,

469
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:56,780
I would gladly lay down my life.

470
00:19:57,240 --> 00:20:00,030
We're finally having some fun.

471
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:08,120
[all grunting]

472
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,710
[Rhyno laughs]

473
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:12,840
[sighs]

474
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,800
[Rhyno exclaims]
The breaking flash seal

475
00:20:20,850 --> 00:20:22,010
was a direct hit.

476
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:24,640
Oh, we make a great team,
don't you agree?

477
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:27,060
-Especially you, my goddess.
-[Teoritta gasps]

478
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:29,150
[RHYNO] Your power
is awe inspiring.

479
00:20:29,190 --> 00:20:30,770
You speak the truth.

480
00:20:30,810 --> 00:20:32,310
Though,
for some strange reason

481
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:35,650
I find myself feeling ambivalent
about your adulation.

482
00:20:35,690 --> 00:20:37,780
[Rhyno laughs]

483
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,860
[RHYNO] No need
to be uncomfortable.

484
00:20:39,910 --> 00:20:42,370
After all, you and I
are one and the same.

485
00:20:42,410 --> 00:20:43,830
[XYLO]
You two are nothing alike.

486
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:46,830
The Holy Knights ought to be
on the move by now.

487
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:48,410
Isn't that right, Venetim?

488
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:50,330
[VENETIM] Uh, oh, yes!

489
00:20:50,370 --> 00:20:53,340
I also secured authorization
for Jayce to join you,

490
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:55,670
and got the underground
waterway locked down.

491
00:20:55,710 --> 00:20:58,470
[XYLO] The waterway?
Was it invaded?

492
00:20:58,510 --> 00:21:01,720
Actually, it was
a spur-of-the-moment suggestion.

493
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,600
[XYLO] You went rogue for that?

494
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:05,850
[RHYNO] Well,
I, for one, approve.

495
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:08,350
We can't be lax in
defending the urban area.

496
00:21:08,730 --> 00:21:10,900
I sent Frenci
and the other night-gaunts

497
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:12,400
to defend that sector.

498
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:14,360
We still don't know
where Spriggan is.

499
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:15,480
[DOTTA] Um, Xylo?

500
00:21:15,570 --> 00:21:18,030
Up ahead and to the right!
On the roofs!

501
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:19,530
This is really bad!

502
00:21:19,570 --> 00:21:20,530
Huh?

503
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:22,280
What are you talking about?

504
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,950
[all mocking]

505
00:21:25,910 --> 00:21:28,200
[RHYNO] They seem
to have lightning staves.

506
00:21:28,250 --> 00:21:30,210
I didn't know they could use
sacred seals.

507
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:33,000
Seriously? Are those damn
coexisters to blame?

508
00:21:33,210 --> 00:21:34,250
Rhyno!

509
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:37,130
[RHYNO] My turn.

510
00:21:40,670 --> 00:21:42,340
[Xylo and Teoritta grunting]

511
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:50,230
[RHYNO] Good. No damage.

512
00:21:50,270 --> 00:21:53,100
Though, it did consume
a fair amount of luminescence.

513
00:21:55,730 --> 00:21:58,780
Dammit all. I would like to duck
into an alley, but these-

514
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:00,950
[RHYNO] We don't have
the luxury of hesitation.

515
00:22:00,990 --> 00:22:02,450
[XYLO] Wait, no!

516
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:08,450
[all gasping]

517
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:15,920
You destroyed all those houses.

518
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:19,710
[RHYNO] Of course, saving lives
takes top priority.

519
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:22,090
That had nothing to do with it.

520
00:22:22,130 --> 00:22:23,590
[RHYNO] Now, onward!

521
00:22:23,630 --> 00:22:26,970
To the people
patiently awaiting salvation!

522
00:22:27,470 --> 00:22:29,270
-[SOLDIER 1] Hurry!
-[SOLDIER 2] Kill them all!

523
00:22:29,310 --> 00:22:30,890
[gunfire]

524
00:22:30,930 --> 00:22:33,190
[SOLDIER 3] Don't let them
get to the Inland District!

525
00:22:33,230 --> 00:22:34,900
[SOLDIER 4] Fire!

526
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:36,940
[monsters screeching]

527
00:22:37,110 --> 00:22:38,940
[SOLDIER 5] Good.
These are the last of them.

528
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:39,940
Fire!

529
00:22:39,980 --> 00:22:41,400
[gunfire]

530
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:45,240
I'm surprised they thought
to lock down the waterway.

531
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:46,780
I wonder
what tipped them off

532
00:22:46,820 --> 00:22:49,790
that we planned to use it
to send in more faeries.

533
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:52,580
I can't help being impressed
by their foresight.

534
00:22:53,290 --> 00:22:55,170
You knights
have earned my praise.

535
00:22:55,210 --> 00:22:57,460
[soldier 1 gasps]
Who's that? Reveal yourself!

536
00:22:57,500 --> 00:23:00,550
[SOLDIER 2]
It's a faerie! Or a human?

537
00:23:00,590 --> 00:23:02,590
[SOLDIER 3] Who are you?
What are you doing here?

538
00:23:02,630 --> 00:23:04,130
Easy does it.

539
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:06,840
I would advise you
not to resist.

540
00:23:07,350 --> 00:23:10,810
To suffer a painful death
is truly pitiable.

541
00:23:11,810 --> 00:23:13,230
[knights gasping]

542
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:22,280
-[slashing]
-[soldiers screaming]

543
00:23:24,440 --> 00:23:26,030
[indistinct chatter]

544
00:23:32,370 --> 00:23:33,370
[KIVIA] Uncle!

545
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:36,330
Patausche,
I'm grateful that you came.

546
00:23:36,370 --> 00:23:39,290
Faeries have been sighted
in the Inland District.

547
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:42,210
Indeed. I received word
of it from the guards.

548
00:23:42,260 --> 00:23:45,090
It would appear they entered
through the waterway.

549
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:58,440
[KIVIA] The military
and the Temple joined forces?

550
00:23:58,480 --> 00:24:01,360
How were you able to coordinate
such a thing, Uncle?

551
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:04,650
This is no time for us to be
feuding amongst ourselves.

552
00:24:04,690 --> 00:24:05,860
What good is a high priest

553
00:24:05,900 --> 00:24:07,820
if he is unable
to bring everyone together

554
00:24:07,860 --> 00:24:09,240
when it matters the most?

555
00:24:09,700 --> 00:24:10,950
It is a blessing.

556
00:24:10,990 --> 00:24:12,700
This peril will strengthen
the bonds

557
00:24:12,740 --> 00:24:14,540
between Temple and military.

558
00:24:14,580 --> 00:24:17,000
And those very bonds
will ensure

559
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:19,500
a path to victory
for all humanity.

560
00:24:19,830 --> 00:24:21,540
Well said, Uncle.

561
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:26,630
Your words are inspiring,
and I will take them to heart.

562
00:24:26,670 --> 00:24:29,180
I will be counting on you,
as ever.

563
00:24:29,220 --> 00:24:31,680
We shall overcome,
if we stick together.

564
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,140
Right.

565
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:34,640
[MARLEN] Hmm.

566
00:24:38,730 --> 00:24:40,850
May the blessings
of Saint Mahaeyzel

567
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:42,060
guide and protect us.

568
00:24:42,110 --> 00:24:43,320
[Kivia gasps]

569
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:47,570
[MARLEN] Now,
let the attack commence.

570
00:24:55,830 --> 00:24:58,500
[Kivia breathes shakily]

